WHY A PREBUILT BINARY, and why this is not a new kind of decision:
wgpu-native set the precedent (engine/vendor/wgpu/VERSION) and this
follows it exactly. The rule the house actually applies is not about a
language -- it is that a dependency must present a stable C ABI AND ship
official prebuilt binaries, so no foreign toolchain enters our build.
wgpu-native passes it and has since GR0; accesskit-c passes it; Taffy
(CSS Grid) publishes zero assets across all releases and therefore does
not, which is why base/gui/SOFTANZA_GUI_PLAN.md 2.1 still refuses grid.
The reasoning is in that plan under "G4b RESOLVED".

WHICH ABI, and why it does not matter: the msvc SHARED build is vendored
rather than the mingw one because it is 352 KB against 5 MB, and no
import library is needed either way -- the DLL is loaded at RUNTIME and
its symbols resolved by name, exactly as stz_gpu does with
wgpu_native.dll. A machine without this file simply has no
screen-reader bridge, which is a legitimate state rather than an error,
the same way a machine without a GPU has no 3D scene.

SIZE, stated because the plan invites the comparison: 352 KB. Section 10
of the GUI plan forbids hand-written platform bridges and calls that
"the 3.47 MB mistake". This is a tenth of it, and someone else
maintains it.

UPDATING: take the same three files from a newer release, replace the
three checksums above, and re-run base/test/gui/gui_a11y_narrated.ring.
The header is generated by cbindgen and the C API is versioned with the
Rust crates, so a minor bump can move entry points -- the guard reads
the version back out of the DLL and prints it.
